      "commit": {
        "author": "\"svc-ci\" <code@example.com>",
        "date": "2026-08-08T08:10:40-05:00",
        "subject": "ci: enable ginkgolinter and fix no-op Eventually assertions (#1902)",
        "body": "* ci: enable ginkgolinter and fix no-op Eventually assertions\n\nEventually without Should() never polls, which made GitRepository\nfinalizer tests flake under load. Enable the linter and fix the\nexisting hits.\n\nCo-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>\nSigned-off-by: Michael Crenshaw <350466+crenshaw-dev@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* test: use a real merge SHA in title-then-merge PullRequest spec\n\nThe fake SCM rejects merge when Spec.MergeSha does not match the source\nbranch HEAD. The deletion Eventually was previously a no-op, so this\nnever failed.\n\nCo-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>\nSigned-off-by: Michael Crenshaw <350466+crenshaw-dev@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* test: point title-then-merge at real branches and clear leftover ginkgolinter hit\n\nThe fake git server only has environment/* refs, so ls-remote of development-next never returned a merge SHA. Rebasing onto main also reintroduced a len() assertion that ginkgolinter rejects.\n\nCo-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>\nSigned-off-by: Michael Crenshaw <350466+crenshaw-dev@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n---------\n\nSigned-off-by: Michael Crenshaw <350466+crenshaw-dev@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>",
        "sha": "582fc17bfb15cd76589208529bc32ce9cac70aba",
        "repoUrl": "https://github.com/argoproj-labs/gitops-promoter"
      }
    }
  ]
}
